k.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["cease","discontinue","blin","turn away from"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2db8be80cbdabbd6f9","definition":"To abandon (someone or something)","example":"I gave up my faith years ago.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["desert","forlet","forsake"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:72012e4097a6053746","definition":"To lose hope concerning (someone or something)","example":"They gave him up for dead.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dcff212979cd4f869f","definition":"To admit defeat, capitulate; to desist for that reason.","example":"OK, I give up, you win.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["capitulate","give in","surrender","throw in the towel","wave the white flag"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:cef403e6c7e75b0640","definition":"To execute a trade on behalf of another broker.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:4b6ee6b73cb23c5f7c","definition":"To acknowledge, recognize as.","example":"The next morning, Sunday, I was boxing with R., who had come over with three or four others to swap a few with me. I was given up to be the best boxer around, and I laid them cold as fast as they came at me.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US, dialectal","register":"US, dialectal, intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:418ccdc5bdd9d1c46f","definition":"To reveal (something).","example":"He gave up that he was the one who opened the door.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US, slang","register":"US, intransitive, slang","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:31982fec557fcbeece","definition":"Become fully taken over by a certain quality, activity, trait, etc.","example":"And now She Seems give up to Sin / Too much neglecting grace within","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"US, dialectal","register":"US, dialectal","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/give_up#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{},"wordFamily":[]}